    "title": "Browser credential or profile store accessed",
    "desc": "A program read a web-browser credential or profile store - Firefox's logins.json / key4.db / cookies.sqlite, Chrome/Chromium's \"Login Data\" / Cookies / Web Data, or a browser profile directory - or ran a known browser-secret dumper (LaZagne). Browsers keep saved passwords, cookies and tokens in these files; reading them harvests credentials and live sessions (MITRE T1555.003), and the same files are what bookmark/history discovery enumerates (MITRE T1217). A browser reading its own store runs as the browser binary, not cat/cp/sqlite3/find over the path, which is what this matches.",
